    <summary>A QBO to PDF converter that reads .qbo and .ofx bank downloads without QuickBooks and saves them as paged PDF statements or Excel-ready CSV on the local PC.</summary>
    <description>This package installs a QBO to PDF converter for Windows PCs in offices that receive .qbo and .ofx bank downloads by email but run no accounting software. Staff get a printable PDF statement or a CSV sheet from each download, and the original file stays unchanged for a later import.

![QBO to PDF Converter screenshot 1](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/b2p/b2p-v4-list.png)

## How to use QBO to PDF Converter Tool

1. Add downloads with Add Files or Add Folder, or drag them in.
2. Select an entry to see which accounts it covers and how its first rows read.
3. Choose PDF for paper or CSV for Excel.
4. Set the date style, then tick the columns you want.
5. Turn on Merge to combine the queue into one result, or leave it off for a file per download.
6. Pick a destination and press Start.

Trial note: an unregistered copy outputs up to 20 transactions from each download and marks the page as a partial result. Registering removes the cap and the mark.

![QBO to PDF Converter screenshot 2](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/b2p/b2p-v4-options.png)

## Convert QBO to PDF or CSV

PDF output follows a statement layout with Date, Check, Payee, Memo and Amount by default, and four extra columns can be ticked. Each account in a download gets its own table, and the footer names the source file and the date the page was produced. CSV output is written in UTF-8 with a BOM and a fixed English header, and formula-like cells are escaped so a spreadsheet does not execute them. When a download holds more than one statement, an Account column is added automatically.

## What stays the same

- A QBO to PDF run only reads the .qbo or .ofx and never rewrites it, so the same copy can still be imported later.
- Bank, card and investment statements are taken from the same file.
- Dates are printed in the style you choose on the Convert page, whatever the bank used.

![QBO to PDF Converter screenshot 3](https://download.softorbits.com/files/pkg-img/b2p/b2p-v4-done.png)

## Who needs a QBO to PDF converter

- Front offices and property managers that receive bank downloads from clients or tenants.
- Small firms that keep paper binders of statements.
- Bookkeepers who convert QBO to PDF and review client downloads on paper before anything is imported.
- Admins who install the tool across several PCs with Chocolatey.

## Trial and license

The package installs the free trial of a commercial program, and a license is required for full use. Lifetime, 1-year and business licenses each remove the 20-transaction cap and the partial-result line. See the [QBO to PDF Converter Tool](https://www.softorbits.net/qbo-to-pdf-converter-software/?utm_source=chocolatey&amp;utm_medium=package) page for details.

## FAQ

### How do I convert a QuickBooks download to PDF?

Add the .qbo file, keep PDF selected and click Start. The statement lands in the folder you chose, readable in any PDF viewer.

### What stops QuickBooks from saving files to PDF?

Usually a damaged PDF component that QuickBooks installs for its own printing. This program has no such dependency, since it writes the PDF from the bank file directly.

### Can I turn an online bank document into a PDF?

Yes, if your online banking offers the statement as a .qbo or .ofx download. Save that file and convert it here.
